	(text "QUIET HEADPHONE PATH (single-ended, one channel)\n\nDAC pins are modelled as +/-1.525 V sources behind 390 ohm (swing is an assumption to confirm).\nVCM is the DAC bias. Real value 1.65 V; drawn as 0 V because the TI OPA161x model does not\nfind a DC operating point with the bias applied. Frequency response and noise are unaffected.\nDrawn in low gain (-20 dB: R9=360, R10=40). For 0 dB gain set R9=1m and R10=1000k.\nRun: Inspect > Simulator > Run. For noise use: .noise v(out) V1 dec 50 20 20k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "13e479fc-4043-46ec-882b-5cf5627895d5")
	)
